24.19.0

# Single source of truth for the Node.js version bundled with Aerini (desktop
# sidecar and the server's Docker image). scripts/fetch-node-binaries.sh and
# the Dockerfile's builder-stage fetch both read this file instead of each
# hardcoding the version separately. Only the first line is parsed; it must
# be a bare semver (e.g. 24.19.0), no "v" prefix, no surrounding text.
#
# Bump triggers:
#   - Node security release affecting the active line (see
#     https://nodejs.org/en/security/ and the nodejs-sec announcement list at
#     https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/nodejs-sec): bump promptly, on
#     its own schedule, not batched with the next planned release.
#   - LTS-to-LTS boundary (e.g. this line's LTS window ending): planned bump,
#     not urgent by itself.
#
# Sandbox dependencies on the bundled Node:
#   aerini-engine/src/nodes/code_node.rs relies on module.registerHooks() (a synchronous,
#   in-thread resolve hook; available from Node 22.15 and 24.0) and on the permission model
#   flag --permission (fs/child-process/worker flags stable from Node 22.17 and 24.2).
#   It no longer uses --experimental-loader or module.register(), the latter deprecated
#   (DEP0205) in favour of registerHooks(). Before bumping, confirm both still exist and that
#   the Code node sandbox self-check still passes (the first sandboxed run reports why if not).
